        "original_id": "c0659ad4-ce50-5a9f-804f-94439bd4600e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ferdinand Zvonimir von Habsburg, Karl von Habsburg, Otto von Habsburg, Princess Regina of Saxe-Meiningen, Charles I\n- Organizations: House of Habsburg-Lorraine\n- Places: Salzburg, Starnberg, Germany, Austria, Bohemia, Croatia, Hungary\n- Roles: head of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine, Austrian politician\n- Topics: Habsburg Monarchy, Empire of Austria, Austro-Hungarian Monarchy, World War I\n\nFacts:\n- Karl von Habsburg was born on 11 January 1961 in Starnberg, Germany.\n- Karl von Habsburg is the son of Otto von Habsburg and Princess Regina of Saxe-Meiningen.\n- Karl von Habsburg is the grandson of Charles I, the last Austrian emperor.\n- Karl von Habsburg is also known as Karl of Austria and is referred to in Austria as Karl Habsburg-Lothringen.\n- Karl von Habsburg is an Austrian politician and the current head of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine.\n- The House of Habsburg-Lorraine ruled the lands of the Habsburg Monarchy, the Empire of Austria, the Austro-Hungarian Monarchy, the Kingdom of Hungary, and the Crown lands of Bohemia and Croatia by hereditary right until the end of World War I.\n- Ferdinand Zvonimir von Habsburg was born on 21 June 1997 in Salzburg.\n- Ferdinand Zvonimir von Habsburg is the eldest son of Karl von Habsburg, the head of the House of Habsburg-Lorraine.",
